.TH UI 4
.SH NAME
ui \- a window of widgets, described through files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ui
[
.B -p
] [
.B -s
.I srvname
]
.PP
.B mount /srv/ui.\fIuser\fP.\fIpid\fP /mnt/ui
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Ui
runs in a window of
.IR wsys (4)
or
.IR rio (1)
and shows there what a client describes: a tree of widgets (rows, columns,
labels, buttons, text boxes, check boxes, switches, menus, progress bars,
sliders, spinners, dividers, images, grids, long lists, scrolled and sized
boxes).
The client writes the tree and reads what the user did; the widgets, their
state (focus, the text being edited, scrolling) and their layout stay in
.IR ui ,
as an
.IR acme (4)
window's text stays in acme.
The files are 9P: a client on another machine mounts them as well
.RI ( import (4)).
.PP
.I Ui
posts its files in
.BI /srv/ srvname
(default
.BI ui. user . pid\fR,
printed on standard output); the entry goes with
.IR ui .
Its widgets are Masonry's (linebender), drawn by vello on the GPU (wgpu's
Vulkan:
.IR gpu (4)
and Mesa) or, without one, by the processor (vello_cpu): no GPU is needed.
.B -p
draws on the processor also with a GPU.
It takes its fonts from
.BR /lib/font/ttf ,
the theme's
.B uifont
first, and its colours from the desktop's theme
.RB ( /dev/theme ,
.IR wsys (4):
the window's background and text, the current border for what is on and
what has the focus, greys between them for the rest; again when it changes;
without
.I wsys
the classic one).
A node's own look (below) goes over the theme's.
.SS Files
.TF nodes/id/children
.TP
.B ctl
Written: a transaction, the lines of one write applied all or none (an error
names the line); read: where the window's contents are on the screen,
.IR "x y width height" .
.TP
.B event
Read: what the user did, a line each, from the open on:
.BI click " id" ,
.BI text " id text"
(a text box changed),
.BI enter " id text" ,
.BI check " id " 0 \fR|\fP 1
(a check box, a switch),
.BI slide " id value" ,
.BI select " id index option" ,
.BR close .
A read waits for one; a flush (an interrupt) ends the wait.
.TP
.B tree
The tree in
.BR ctl 's
language: written to
.B ctl
it makes the same scene.
.TP
.B renderer
What draws the window:
.BI gpu " adapter"
or
.BR cpu .
.TP
.BI nodes/ id /kind
The node's kind.
.TP
.BI nodes/ id /props
Its properties,
.I key value
a line; written:
.B set
for each line.
.TP
.BI nodes/ id /children
.TP
.BI nodes/ id /rect
Where it is in the window,
.I x0 y0 x1 y1
(as the last frame had it; empty without a widget, as a long list's children
not shown).
.TP
.BI nodes/ id /image
An image node's picture: written, PNG or
.IR image (6)
(compressed or not, any channels), shown when the file is closed (a picture
it cannot read: the close's error); read, its width and height.
.PD
.SS Ctl's language
.TF "move id parent [index]"
.TP
.BI new " id kind \fR[\fPparent \fR[\fPindex\fR]]"
A node of a kind:
.BR column ,
.BR row ,
.BR label ,
.BR button ,
.BR textbox ,
.BR checkbox ,
.BR progress ,
.BR slider ,
.B scroll
(one child),
.B box
(one child or none),
.B list
(any number of children in a column that scrolls; only those it shows have
widgets, so a list of thousands costs what a screenful does; the others have
no
.BR rect ),
.B grid
(its children row by row in
.B columns
columns, default 2: a table),
.B image
(its picture written to
.IB nodes/ id /image ),
.B select
(a menu:
.B options
separated by
.BR | ,
the
.B selected
one's index),
.BR switch ,
.B divider
(across a column;
.B axis
.B vertical
in a row),
.BR spinner ;
in
.I parent
(default
.BR root ,
a column) at
.I index
(default: the end).
Ids are letters, digits and
.BR _-. .
.TP
.BI set " id key value"
A property; the value is the rest of the line (in rc's quotes if it starts or
ends with blanks):
.B text
(label, button, text box, check box),
.B placeholder
(text box),
.B checked
(0 or 1),
.B value
(progress: 0 to 1 or
.BR none ;
slider),
.BR min ,
.BR max ,
.B step
(slider),
.BR width ,
.B height
(box, in pixels),
.B flex
(a child's share of its row or column),
.B gap
(between a row's or column's children, in pixels; else the theme's)
and
.B align
.RB ( start ,
.BR center ,
.BR end :
across a row or column).
.IP
And for a node of any kind its look (else the theme's):
.B background
and
.B border
(colours,
.BI # rrggbb
or
.BI # rrggbbaaR),
.BR borderwidth ,
.B radius
(of the corners) and
.B padding
(pixels),
.B color
(a label's text, a divider's line).
.B animate
.I ms
makes a progress bar's or slider's
.BR value ,
a box's
.B width
and
.B height
go to a new one in
.I ms
milliseconds, slow at both ends, a frame at a time in
.I ui
(the client writes the new value once, also over the network; the tree has it at once).
.TP
.BI del " id
The node and what is under it.
.TP
.BI move " id parent \fR[\fPindex\fR]
.TP
.BI title " text
.TP
.B clear
All but the root.
.PD
.PP
The user's changes go into the tree as well: a text box's
.BR text ,
a check box's
.BR checked ,
a slider's
.BR value .
.SH EXAMPLES
A window with a button, from rc:
.IP
.EX
window 'ui -s hello'
mount /srv/hello /mnt/ui
echo 'new b button
set b text press me' >/mnt/ui/ctl
cat /mnt/ui/event	# click b, when it is pressed
.EE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TF UIDEBUG
.TP
.B UIDEBUG
The window's events, Masonry's signals and what wgpu logs, on standard error.
.PD
